dge` text `#a3271d` on the card background `#fff` (the badge\n222:- `.due-date-clear` text `#5a646c` on `#fff`: **6.04:1** \u2014 passes.\n224:`#ccd2d6` borders on `.due-date-input`/`.due-date-clear` are the same\n235:  \"Overdue\" \u2014 the `\u26a0` glyph is `aria-hidden=\"true\"` and purely decorative,\n242:  present) \u2192 overdue badge (not focusable, it's `role=\"status\"`, not\n245:- **Target size:** `.due-date-clear` uses the same padding as\n249:- **Live update:** the badge's `role=\"status\"` means a due-date edit that\n250:  causes a task to newly become (or stop being) overdue is announced to\n259:| 1 | AddTask due-date input defaults to `''` \u2192 sent as `null`; nothing required to submit. |\n260:| 2 | AddTask due-date input value flows through `onAdd` \u2192 row displays it via `.due-date-input` bound to `task.due_date`. |\n261:| 3 | Row `.due-date-input` (`onChange`) sets/changes; `.due-date-clear` (shown only when set) clears to `null`. |\n262:| 4 | `.overdue-badge` \u2014 text \"Overdue\" + decorative icon, not colour-only; contrast computed above. |\n263:| 5 | `isOverdue()` uses `<` (strict), so a due date equal to today's local date renders the \"future/not overdue\" row layout. |\n264:| 6 | `isOverdue()` short-circuits `false` on `due_date == null`; future dates fail the `<` check. |\n265:| 7 | `isOverdue()` is gated on `!task.done` \u2014 done-task wireframe above shows the badge absent regardless of stored date. |\n271:- No due-date column/sort, no due-date filter chip alongside", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Sg5PKxTp8pbSTN912Nw4vV", "session_id": "7e8d71f9-876f-4f66-9eef-834cc1faa181"}}
