{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:50:02Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 150, "kind": "message", "text": "## Review: Taiga #12 \u2014 Give tasks a due date (attempt 2)\n\n**Context confirmed:** the reviewer's attempt-1 blocker (`TypeError: Object of type date is not JSON serializable` in `store.py:47`) is fixed via `task.model_dump(mode=\"json\")`. I re-ran the full suite myself rather than trusting the developer's report.\n\n**Verification run this session:**\n- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 **47 passed**, 0 failures.\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 clean build, no errors.\n- `git status --porcelain` \u2192 only the 12 expected modified files, no stray untracked files.\n\n**Diff reviewed in full:** `backend/app/{main,models,store}.py`, `backend/tests/{test_tasks,test_persistence}.py`, `frontend/src/{App.jsx,api.js}`, `frontend/src/components/{AddTask,TaskList}.jsx`, `frontend/src/App.css`, plus `docs/{spec,design}.md`.\n\n**Spec/design fidelity check (all 9 ACs):**\n- AC1/2 (optional on create) \u2014 `AddTask.jsx` defaults `dueDate=''`, maps `'' \u2192 null`, covered by `test_create_defaults_to_no_due_date`.\n- AC3 (set/change/clear from row) \u2014 `TaskList.jsx` `.due-date-input` + `.due-date-clear` button, covered by `test_clearing_an_existing_due_date`.\n- AC4 (overdue marked by more than colour) \u2014 `.overdue-badge` renders visible text \"Overdue\" plus `aria-hidden` icon; matches `docs/design.md`'s contrast computations.\n- AC5/AC6 (today and future not overdue) \u2014 `isOverdue` uses strict `<` against `todayISO()`; ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` strings compare lexicographically identically to chronological order, so this is correct without needing `Date` parsing.\n- AC7 (done suppresses badge) \u2014 `isOverdue` is gated on `!task.done`.\n- AC8 (malformed date \u2192 422) \u2014 `DueDateIn.due_date: date | None` (required key, nullable value) rejects garbage via Pydantic; covered by two dedicated tests, both passing.\n- AC9 (survives restart) \u2014 `test_due_date_absent_survives_a_simulated_restart` plus the updated existing persistence test, both passing.\n\n**Route ordering** (`main.py:48` `/due-date` before `main.py:56` generic `/{task_id}` PATCH) correctly avoids shadowing, following the same pattern as the pre-existing `/priority` route.\n\n**Store mutation pattern** (`store.py:81-87` `set_due_date`) is byte-for-byte the same shape as `set_priority`/`set_done`/`update_title` \u2014 no new idiom introduced.\n\n## Will block\nNone.\n\n## Will comment\nNone.\n\n## Worth considering\n- Frontend has no test infrastructure at all (`frontend/package.json` has no `test` script, no test files anywhere in the repo) despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test`. This is a pre-existing, project-wide gap \u2014 not introduced or worsened by this diff \u2014 and was already noted as out-of-scope in the design stage's precedent (the priority feature shipped the same way). Not this cycle's responsibility to fix.\n\nVERDICT: approve", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "7e8d71f9-876f-4f66-9eef-834cc1faa181"}}
